{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1402235-sheriff-during-mardi-gras","id":1402235,"title":"Sheriff during mardi gras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-11T06:52:53-07:00","id":1402235,"title":"Sheriff during mardi gras","content":"It's been awhile but i need some ideas again. We're close to Mardi gras in our upcoming game and as the sheriff I've been placed in charge of the domains security. <br /> <br /> I've only been the sheriff for less than 3 months and have yet to really establish myself or a strong powerbase. <br /> <br /> Now I have to come up with ideas to secure the domain for both local and visiting kindred. Any ideas to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25838-dart93","name":"Dart93","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T08:36:09-07:00","id":1402253,"title":"","content":"The Sheriff does NOT do his work alone. You need a strategy and then resources and hounds to make it work. Since you are the Sheriff the Prince and/or the Primogen council should<br /> <br /> First thing: do you have the political support to pull off the job set for you? Is the Prince helping or is he settimg you up to fail? Who on the Primogen council is working with you? Who's against you? The answers to these questions should give you an idea of what you can reasonably expect, possibly identifying and thus discouraging troublemakers from making their move during the festivities.<br /> <br /> Second: you need a list of the kindred who will be allowed in the city during Mardi Gras. Each one should have a profile and you should know what to expect by any of them, assigning personnel to deal with their needs/defend them/keep them in check. This is the ideal situation but you probably won't have the resources needed to keep everything and everyone under control, therefore...<br /> <br /> Third: ... set up easy to follow rules. Make clear what are the places where kindred are allowed to hunt and the places where they cannot. Describe behaviours that are acceptable and encouraged and behaviours that will be punished. Make the Prince and the Primogen council sanction your edicts so no one can retroactively say you are doing things on your own and abusing your position.<br /> <br /> Fourth: plan for the unexpected. What if the inquisition attacks during the festivities? What if one of the kindred frezies? Are you prepared for a Sabbat incursion? Make sure to have contingency plans for all these possible situations and more, also share them with your hounds and ghouls (assuming you can trust them) and let them know what to do in case these scenarios happen.<br /> <br /> Fifth: Keep in mind what Von Molkte's lesson: &quot;No plan of operations extends with any certainty beyond the first contact with the main hostile force&quot; (shorter version: &quot;No plan survives contact with the enemy&quot;). You cannot plan for everything, and amount of planning is well and good but it's likely at a certain point you will need to improvise. Be ready to do so effectively and choose people who can keep a cool head under stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T10:24:48-07:00","id":1402268,"title":"","content":"Are their mages in the Chronicle? With Mardi Gras,if this is New Orleans, there will be other attendees. I could expect mages who didn't like vampires to come in with the mass of regular humans and cause trouble once they get into the city. That would be especially true if you have any voodoo-themed events in the area, because most of the voodoo-practicing mages have some strong anti-vampire factions.<br /> <br /> Be sure to have mortal security that isn't clearly connected to you tied in to your network. That way, the mortal security can handle the regular revelers and if something goes nuts, you're going to get a heads-up. Have connections and communications that are both physical and electronic. Physical won't be as fast, because few things run at the speed of sound, but a runner could be useful. Maybe a couple of cabbies or delivery drivers who can quickly get to your people if there's a problem in their area. For electronic communication, it can be spoofed and intercepted. Take precautions, because some jerk with the ability to make you think there's a problem in one area with a radio call for security help might be doing that as a diversion so they can hit their real target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}